SUMMARY:Rooted at Spreckels Performing Arts Center
DESCRIPTION:Rooted at Spreckels Performing Arts Center is a heartwarming comedy by Deborah Zoe Laufer about family\, love\, and finding purpose. The story follows Emery\, who lives in an isolated treehouse surrounded by plants\, while her sister Hazel struggles to support her lifestyle. When Emery’s plant experiment videos unexpectedly go viral and inspire a devoted following\, their lives take an unexpected turn. As chaos unfolds\, three women must reconsider their choices and discover what truly brings meaning to their lives. This entertaining production explores the messy\, fierce connections that keep people grounded.  &lt;bR.  Rooted runs November 27 through December 13\, 2026\, with Friday and Saturday performances at 7:30 PM and Sunday matinees at 2 PM. Opening night on November 27.
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/rooted-at-spreckels-performing-arts-center/
LOCATION:5409 Snyder Lane, Rohnert Park, CA, 94928, United States
GEO:-122.687524;38.3440562
CATEGORIES:Family Friendly,Performing Arts,Sonoma County
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://winecountry-media.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2026/11/20125310/1-4.png
END:VEVENT
